# A slow taper keeps the light in the fundamental mode; a fast one scatters it into higher modes.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title Taper from 0.5 to 3 um over 40 um
reference 2.75
window width=20 length=60
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide taper x=0 w0=0.5 w1=3 from=10 to=50
guide straight x=0 width=3 from=50 to=60
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=60 x=0 width=3
plane end z=60
expect power out 0.997663821 2e-7
expect total end 0.999955678 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.0000000 2e-6
expect radius end 1.1401597 2e-6
expect neff 2.779621697 2e-8
